    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Josh Lowe** (71.68). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Young, where a favorable platoon dynamic and a prime spot in the two-hole elevate his efficiency. Similarly, **Josh Lowe** capitalizes on the elevated xERA of Sasaki; despite hitting seventh, his strong situational metrics against a right-handed arm make him an essential start. While **Kyle Tucker** (67.71) remains a constant force, the combination of **Drake Baldwin** (66.59) leading off and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.93) protecting the middle of the order provides the necessary depth to compete in both power and run production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the ledger was the choice to bench **Dominic Smith** (56.82) and **Coby Mayo** (56.80), both of whom hovered near the threshold of our starting unit. **Dominic Smith** was bypassed primarily because his base efficiency lacked the high-end sprint speed profile we prioritize to chase stolen bases, a category where our roster remains lean. We also face a specific risk with **Jackson Merrill** (56.95); while he carries a strong score, his status remains \"Lineup Pending.\" Should he drop in the order or be rested, the efficiency drop-off against a high-caliber arm like George Kirby is significant. Additionally, while **Sam Antonacci** (58.32) remains in the lineup due to his elite 0.400 xwOBA, we are monitoring the wind-in conditions at his venue, which poses a slight downward risk to his power projections today.",
